        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1159768c-4590-3c73-bb4d-8f28f67bcbde",
                "word": "cishet",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "519c032b-a557-38f1-b1b4-f72149e2a380",
                        "entry_id": "1159768c-4590-3c73-bb4d-8f28f67bcbde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cisgender and heterosexual."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f45cf66d-72f1-4475-9408-334840937e59",
                                "sense_id": "519c032b-a557-38f1-b1b4-f72149e2a380",
                                "text": "Even in death, the way we are spoken about by the mainstream cishet world is traumatizing and violent. Even in death, trans women of color cannot escape the trauma of colonialism and genocide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "808ce3bf-5537-42d1-9c16-06c1dd049412",
                                "sense_id": "519c032b-a557-38f1-b1b4-f72149e2a380",
                                "text": "While children can be born to any kind of parent and situation, unless drastic measures are taken, they will be raised in an overwhelmingly cisgendered and heterosexual (cishet) world. Cishet children and adults’ identities are affirmed by media, legal documents, population majority, history and other depictions of assumed cis-ness and heterosexuality."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cb77367-c440-4858-86b4-ca4d13377432",
                                "sense_id": "519c032b-a557-38f1-b1b4-f72149e2a380",
                                "text": "[…] it reinforces the problematic notion that 'true' feminism belongs to cishet white abled feminists; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7dcdd107-177b-45bd-823e-ced8d5f8d191",
                        "source_entry_id": "1159768c-4590-3c73-bb4d-8f28f67bcbde",
                        "source_sense_id": "519c032b-a557-38f1-b1b4-f72149e2a380",
                        "source_sense_description": "cisgender and heterosexual",
                        "target_lang_word": "cishet",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cishet",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0823db59-1a7e-37d1-b8ed-20fc3ce47968",
                                        "entry_id": "1693ffd4-3bd9-398d-b924-9fa08dd89f56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif aux personnes qui sont à la fois cis (c’est-à-dire non trans) et hétérosexuelles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49024f51-efc5-4955-8055-d3985d100f2a",
                                                "sense_id": "0823db59-1a7e-37d1-b8ed-20fc3ce47968",
                                                "text": "Tolérance. Cela voudrait donc dire que nous sommes différent.es de la norme de par notre identité de genre ou notre orientation sexuelle mais que les personnes cishet ont la bonté d’accepter notre présence dans leur environnement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cishet",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fbf5743-fde0-352d-a2c1-b156201c927f",
                                        "entry_id": "51b069fb-f424-31ff-9145-7903334f1e21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui vit dans le genre correspondant à son sexe et est attirée par des personnes d’un autre genre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc0514ee-a70a-40cb-8401-0015b8d27d3e",
                                                "sense_id": "7fbf5743-fde0-352d-a2c1-b156201c927f",
                                                "text": "Le fétichisme que nous subissons est malsain, je le subis moi-même, ayant fait la grossière erreur de relationner avec des mecs cishet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd595678-62dc-4755-8c91-e0d340b0cf87",
                                                "sense_id": "7fbf5743-fde0-352d-a2c1-b156201c927f",
                                                "text": "Il y a encore quelques jours j’ai vu passer un tweet d’un mec qui s’est fait tabasser par des cishet en soirée gay. Et ça, je suis désolé, mais ce n’est plus tolérable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
